Great — Wed 13:00 PT works for us. Adding details below and a short snippet inlined; Dev and Dylan will cover the deeper runtime bits on the call. 

Schema updates: we'll add the optional "notes" (maxLength: 2048) and "source_document_id" (string) to v1. I'll attach v1.1 after Dev updates the schema.

Validation vs decoding errors (high-level):
- Constrained decoding failures (model returns malformed JSON or missing required fields): treat as transient decode error — attempt up to 2 deterministic retries with a slightly different decoding temperature/penalties, then fall back to a safety-path that returns a structured failure object to your service (status: "decode_failed").
- Validation failures (payload parses as JSON but fails schema validation): do NOT retry automatically. These are semantic errors — surface them to your business logic with full validation error details; you can choose to queue for human review or apply a corrective auto-rewrite flow (we can propose one in the call).

SDK snippet (Node, simplified):
```
// pseudo-code snippet — Redwood Node SDK
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_KEY });
const resp = await client.generateStructured({
  model: 'gpt-structured-1',
  input: prompt,
  decoding: { mode: 'constrained_json', schema: './acme_schema_req_v1.1.json' },
  hooks: {
    onDecodeFailure: async (ctx) => {
      // automatic deterministic retry up to 2 times
      if (ctx.retries < 2) return { retry: true, adjust: { temperature: 0 } };
      return { retry: false, fallback: { status: 'decode_failed', errors: ctx.errors } };
    },
    onValidationError: (errors) => {
      // send to validation queue / surface to service
      sendToQueue('validation-errors', { errors, payload: ctx.payload });
    }
  }
});
```

Recommended server-side validation: use a JSON Schema validator (Ajv for Node, jsonschema or fastjsonschema for Python). We'll include sample validation error payloads in the updated doc.

